  "testCoverage": [
    "Actual runReferenceHandler success using hard mocks for process spawning and launch-owner acquisition.",
    "Owner acquisition delay exceeds the configured test execution timeout while the successful handler completes within the fresh unchanged deadline.",
    "Actual execution timeout plus failed native-state inspection reports execution-timeout then cleanup-unconfirmed.",
    "Observer exceptions preserve successful outputs, failure codes, and expected cleanup calls.",
    "Cleanup-only delay beyond the execution budget does not report an execution timeout after the execution phase completed.",
    "Absolute-deadline check marks timeout once when synchronous dispatch crosses the deadline before the timer callback.",
    "Malformed handler protocol retains FRAME_ACCESS when cleanup succeeds; existing cleanup failure precedence retains LIMIT when cleanup cannot validate state."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No actual Docker/native execution or service interaction.",
    "No browser/build/inventory/full integration test.",
    "This diagnostic patch does not identify the hosted LIMIT cause or claim it fixes it."
  ],
